YAML STRUCTURE:
The workflow MUST follow this exact structural pattern:

name: CI
on:
  push:
    branches:
    - {{ analysis.default_branch }}
  pull_request:
    branches:
    - {{ analysis.default_branch }}
permissions:
  contents: read
concurrency:
  group: {% raw %}${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}{% endraw %}
  cancel-in-progress: true
jobs:
  <job definitions here>

JOB ORGANIZATION:
{% if analysis.build_command and analysis.test_command %}
Use TWO jobs:
  1. A "build" job with steps: checkout, setup runtime, install dependencies, build.
  2. A "test" job (needs: build) with steps: checkout, setup runtime, install dependencies, run tests, upload results.
{% elif analysis.build_command %}
Use a SINGLE "build" job with steps: checkout, setup runtime, install dependencies, build. Do NOT include test steps.
{% elif analysis.test_command %}
Use a SINGLE "test" job with steps: checkout, setup runtime, install dependencies, run tests, upload results.
{% else %}
